					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/captain-kirby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3440103); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3440103&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605795276" alt="Captain Kirby" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3440103)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/captain-kirby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3440103); return false;" >Captain Kirby</a></span> <span class="odate time_1560130184 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">10 Jun 2019 01:29</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4276231">
									

<p>There are parts of this that I like, but there's a lot of things here that just really bother me.</p>
<p>The first thing that I noticed when reading this is that there's a lot of repetition between the fragments. There's not much that actually changes between the fragments just in terms of words. Usually about half of the words seem to remain the same (I haven't done the math, but I think half isn't too far off). My issue with this is that like, as a reader I started scanning to find what's different. It felt less like I was trying to read through the whole document and more like I was trying to just find what's changed. I think this could be easily fixed by like, just highlighting the changed bits in blue, although there's a large part of me that wishes there was just a more substantial change between each fragment. I say this because right now, while I do believe you have an intended reason why you divide each of the fragments up like this, it's really hard for me to figure out what is so important about the difference between the boarded up version, and the sealed version.</p>
<p>The other thing that bothers me is the video. It's a really nice video. Like, I like it a lot. But I feel like it doesn't actually like&#8230; give me any new information in and of itself. The bit at the very end is just a reference to something you effectively tell the reader in the second to last fragment, and like&#8230; unless you're much more clever than I'm giving you credit for, the leading 2 minutes of that clip appear to be just atmosphere effectively? Like I couldn't discern any details that really changed my understanding or intuition behind the story you're trying to tell. It does a really good job at building ambiance, but I guess I'm really just echoing ARD's point that you don't really do anything with the tension it builds.</p>
<p>Finally&#8230; why did you end it with that emoticon? I'm really curious about this because any form of emoticon feels really tonally dissonant from the mood you've built throughout the rest of the piece. Like, it feels playful and mischievous, but not in a way that contrasts well with the video that precedes it (at least in my opinion). I'm very curious why you put it there, because I have the feeling there's a specific reason and I'm just not getting it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
